[2026-03-14T22:15:52.678Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FZy3wn4Xei6yUiHmBNh6qV","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've found all the information you requested. Here's a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Test Spec Entries in docs/tests.md\n\nAll 20 test cases you listed are present in the Create Issue Modal section of `/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md` (lines 1326-1424). Here's the breakdown:\n\n### Dropdown/Selector Tests\n1. **Cycle dropdown shows team's available cycles** (lines 1326-1329)\n2. **Cycle dropdown allows selecting a cycle** (lines 1331-1334)\n3. **Cycle dropdown updates when team is changed** (lines 1336-1339)\n4. **Due date picker allows selecting a date** (lines 1341-1344)\n5. **Due date picker allows clearing the date** (lines 1346-1349)\n6. **Parent issue selector is searchable** (lines 1351-1354)\n7. **Parent issue selector allows selecting a parent** (lines 1356-1359)\n8. **Assignee selector can be used multiple times** (lines 1361-1364)\n9. **Labels selector can be used multiple times in sequence** (lines 1366-1369)\n10. **Status dropdown can be changed multiple times** (lines 1371-1374)\n\n### Action Button Tests\n11. **Create Issue button is visible and styled** (lines 1378-1380)\n12. **Cancel button is visible** (lines 1382-1384)\n13. **Cancel button closes the modal** (lines 1386-1389)\n14. **Cancel button discards form data** (lines 1391-1394)\n15. **Create Issue button submits the form with all fields** (lines 1396-1399)\n16. **Create Issue with only required fields** (lines 1401-1404)\n\n### Issue Creation & Integration Tests\n17. **Created issue appears in the team issues list** (lines 1406-1409)\n18. **Created issue with parent appears as sub-issue** (lines 1411-1414)\n19. **Created issue generates activity history entry** (lines 1416-1419)\n20. **Created issue generates inbox notification for assignee** (lines 1421-1424)\n\n---\n\n## Existing Test File Patterns\n\n### 1. **create-issue-modal-form.spec.ts** (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/create-issue-modal-form.spec.ts`)\n**Pattern Focus:** Form field rendering, validation, and basic input handling\n- Uses shared helpers for login and modal opening\n- Tests field visibility with `toBeVisible()`\n- Tests field labels with `toContainText()`\n- Tests form submission and validation errors\n- Tests dropdown options with `getByTestId()` filters\n- Each test opens the modal fresh via helper function\n\n**Key helpers used:**\n- `loginViaApi()` - handles authentication\n- `openCreateModalFromTeamPage()` - navigates and opens modal with team context\n- Uses `expect().toBeVisible()`, `expect().toHaveValue()`, `expect().toContainText()`\n\n**Test structure example:**\n```typescript\ntest('Title field is required', async ({ page, baseURL }) => {\n  await openCreateModalFromTeamPage(page, baseURL!);\n  await page.getByTestId('create-issue-submit-btn').click();\n  await expect(page.getByTestId('create-issue-title-error')).toBeVisible();\n  await expect(page.getByTestId('create-issue-modal')).toBeVisible();\n});\n```\n\n### 2. **create-issue-modal-selectors.spec.ts** (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/create-issue-modal-selectors.spec.ts`)\n**Pattern Focus:** Multi-select dropdowns, searchable fields, and label/selector interactions\n- Tests dropdown visibility and option rendering\n- Tests search/filter functionality in selectors\n- Tests multi-select with multiple selections and removals\n- Tests label badge removal\n- Uses similar helper structure as form tests\n\n**Key patterns:**\n- Dropdown visibility checked with `getByTestId()`\n- Options filtered with `.locator('button').filter({ hasText: /text/ })`\n- Search inputs filled with `.fill()`\n- Multiple selections tested in sequence\n- Badge removal tested with locator chaining\n\n**Test structure example:**\n```typescript\ntest('Assignee selector allows selecting a member', async ({ page, baseURL }) => {\n  await loginAndOpenCreateModal(page, baseURL!);\n  await expect(page.getByTestId('create-issue-assignee-selector')).toContainText('No assignee');\n  await page.getByTestId('create-issue-assignee-selector').click();\n  await expect(page.getByTestId('create-issue-assignee-dropdown')).toBeVisible();\n  await page.getByTestId('create-issue-assignee-search').fill('Bob');\n  const bobOption = page.getByTestId('create-issue-assignee-dropdown').locator('button').filter({ hasText: /Bob Smith/ });\n  await expect(bobOption).toBeVisible({ timeout: 10000 });\n  await bobOption.click();\n  await expect(page.getByTestId('create-issue-assignee-selector')).toContainText('Bob Smith');\n});\n```\n\n### 3. **team-issues-create.spec.ts** (`/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/team-issues-create.spec.ts`)\n**Pattern Focus:** End-to-end issue creation and list integration\n- Tests modal opening from team issues page\n- Tests actual issue creation and appearance in list\n- Counts issues before/after creation\n- Tests success indicators\n- Uses slowdown for time-intensive operations with `test.slow()`\n\n**Key patterns:**\n- Navigation to team issues page\n- Issue count verification with `toHaveCount()`\n- Data-testid patterns like `[data-testid^=\"issue-row-\"]` for multiple elements\n- Success indicators checked with `toBeVisible()`\n- Modal closure verified with `toHaveCount(0)`\n- Uses timestamps in test data to ensure uniqueness\n\n**Test structure example:**\n```typescript\ntest('Newly created issue appears in the list', async ({ page, baseURL }) => {\n  test.slow();\n  await loginAndNavigateToTeamIssues(page, baseURL!);\n  await expect(page.getByTestId('team-issues-list')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n  const initialRows = page.locator('[data-testid^=\"issue-row-\"]');\n  await expect(initialRows).toHaveCount(8, { timeout: 30000 });\n  // ... create issue ...\n  await expect(page.getByTestId('create-issue-success')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n  await expect(page.locator('[data-testid^=\"issue-row-\"]')).toHaveCount(initialCount + 1, { timeout: 30000 });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Testing Patterns Across All Files\n\n1. **Helper functions for setup** - Shared login, navigation, and modal opening\n2. **Test data from seed** - Uses predefined teams (ENG, DES), users, issues, and projects\n3. **Generous timeouts** - Default `{ timeout: 30000 }` for page visibility waits\n4. **Data-testid selectors** - All UI elements identified with kebab-case test IDs\n5. **Chained locators** - `.filter()`, `.locator()` for complex element selection\n6. **Assertions with context** - Tests both state and UI appearance (icons, styling)\n7. **API-based authentication** - Login handled via fetch to `/api/login` rather than form filling"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a2f1bb0fbe6c5097e (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 33115\ntool_uses: 9\nduration_ms: 20470</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c91b507-8d26-43b3-bb1c-ff396945621b","uuid":"17e675e3-b5b9-49d2-a5c4-3b830cb0eb49","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /repo/apps/LinearClone, I need to find the test spec entries for these specific tests in docs/tests.md:\n1. Cycle dropdown shows team's available cycles\n2. Cycle dropdown allows selecting a cycle\n3. Cycle dropdown updates when team is changed\n4. Due date picker allows selecting a date\n5. Due date picker allows clearing the date\n6. Parent issue selector is searchable\n7. Parent issue selector allows selecting a parent\n8. Assignee selector can be used multiple times\n9. Labels selector can be used multiple times in sequence\n10. Status dropdown can be changed multiple times\n11. Create Issue button is visible and styled\n12. Cancel button is visible\n13. Cancel button closes the modal\n14. Cancel button discards form data\n15. Create Issue button submits the form with all fields\n16. Create Issue with only required fields\n17. Created issue appears in the team issues list\n18. Created issue with paren